## Why This Is Asked

Real-time voice UIs in field apps require efficient native modules, cross-platform bridging, and careful threading and privacy considerations. This question probes practical design, API ergonomics, and trade-offs under latency and power constraints.

## Key Concepts

- React Native TurboModules/JSI bridging
- Real-time DSP: noise suppression, echo cancellation
- Dedicated DSP/native thread and backpressure
- Cross-platform audio pipelines (iOS/Android)
- Privacy and battery considerations, permission flows

## Code Example

```javascript
// useVoiceCapture hook outline (RN side)
function useVoiceCapture(onFrame) {
  useEffect(() => {
    NativeVoiceModule.startCapture({ sampleRate: 16000, channels: 1 });
    const sub = NativeVoiceModule.onFrame(({ frame, ts }) => onFrame(frame, ts));
    return () => { sub.remove(); NativeVoiceModule.stopCapture(); };
  }, [onFrame]);
}
```

